================================================================================
ARCHITECTURE / PARITY NOTES
================================================================================
* Data binds through the `@Observable DriveDetailPageModel` (ADR-004 -- no networking in the
  view); the web hooks map 1:1 to the `DriveDetailDataSource` seam:
    useDrive(id)               -> loadDrive(driveID)             GET /drives/{id}
    useVehicle(vehicleId)      -> loadVehicle(vehicleID)         GET /vehicles/{id}
    useDriveWhyEnded(id,w,en)  -> loadWhyEnded(driveID, window)  GET /drives/{id}/why-ended
* Everything is stored SI (m / m/s / Wh / W / degC / kPa -- phase-42/48 canonical) and converted
  ONLY at the SwiftUI render boundary via the shared `Units` facade (P1/S5) + `TS*` SI formatter
  components (ADR-005). Stats are computed in SI; the display-only ratios the web keeps
  (consumption Wh/km->Wh/mi, efficiency %/100) convert at the boundary exactly as the web page.
* Every web `<SectionErrorBoundary fallbackTitle=…>` is reproduced by `DriveDetailSectionBoundary`
  (SwiftUI has no render-time catch, so the failed condition is supplied by the model) -- so all
  19 section fallback titles + the title/vehicle/no-telemetry strings resolve from the catalog.
* Every web region is reproduced: header, no-telemetry banner, 5 hero gauges, timeline, 8 stat
  cards, AI coaching, more-details, energy-summary, cost-savings, route map, journey-details, the
  overview/SoC/elevation/temperature/speed-histogram/power/tire charts, AI speed insights, and the
  lazy why-ended diagnostic.
* Charts use ONLY the P3 native Swift Charts wrappers (TSLineChart / TSAreaChart / TSBarChart /
  TSComposedChart) -- never a web view. The 5 hero RadialGauges use a feature-local
  `DriveMetricGauge` (token-built ring) so the absolute value+unit render like the web gauge.
* The route map uses the P3 MapKit wrapper `TSMapView` (route polyline + start/end annotations +
  TSMapLayerSwitcher) with the speed-band legend thresholds converted to the user's speed unit.
* Navigation: `/drives/:id` is modeled as a typed NavigationDestination (`DriveDetailLink(driveID:)`
  + `.driveDetailDestination()`), mirroring the accepted unrouted-detail precedent
  `ChargingDetailRouteRegistration` -- no widening of the value-less `AppRoute` enum.
* Adaptive macOS + iOS (ADR-002/006): gauge/stat/tile grids reflow (LazyVGrid adaptive columns);
  the chart pairs sit side-by-side at regular width and stack at compact width (AdaptiveChartPair);
  the system back button + ShareLink replace the web back/print/share affordances; light/dark +
  Dynamic Type + VoiceOver honored (accessibilityLabel/Value on gauges, charts, panels).
* Three data states implemented for every source: loading -> redaction skeleton (Chrome); error ->
  retry surface; empty -> ContentUnavailableView per chart/panel + the no-telemetry banner
  envelope (NoTelemetryDriveDetailDataSource preview drives it).
* A type-name collision with the pre-existing `WhyEndedPanel` surface (which already declares
  `DriveDiagnosticWindow`) was resolved by naming this page's enum `DriveDetailDiagnosticWindow`
  -- the new code stays self-contained and does not depend on the legacy surface (per the
  no-legacy-coupling rule).

